#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cec0e48f-9fbb-5ada-b7fd-0d389d1b7438" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem for a Decoupled Linear System of First-Order ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fc921c2-7d6d-5630-b287-3b5944fe1d44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368982} {:answer/id #uuid "ee7f3b8f-7089-56b8-bdc2-7d5345a7bfd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{2}^{-t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{7}t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368983} {:answer/id #uuid "e434fe7d-a529-5830-ab6a-da9d8215ba4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{7}t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368984} {:answer/id #uuid "76a6a07f-0247-5980-a494-e450296786dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{2}^{-t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{7}^{t/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368985} {:answer/id #uuid "45841a2c-8a62-555c-9a04-0c7f4d369a82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{7}t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee7f3b8f-7089-56b8-bdc2-7d5345a7bfd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{2}^{-t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{7}t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368983} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c018f2c-e2bb-5b45-8cfe-2c4088ad8b80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a203314-ffdc-5f7d-a0f6-f9522124d05e" :question/math-academy-id "q-332716" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{7}\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We have a decoupled system. Therefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{7}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{2}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{7}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =9\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{2}^{-t}+(-5)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{7}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{2}^{-t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{7}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167253 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cec0e48f-9fbb-5ada-b7fd-0d389d1b7438" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem for a Decoupled Linear System of First-Order ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0bd0fc6-bb96-5a85-9066-598aa3452b77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368988} {:answer/id #uuid "0d42b8e5-9889-57b9-a7fe-b6ca1e22490d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368989} {:answer/id #uuid "2fe1efaf-8ee8-5c9b-84c1-abd191edf30b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368990} {:answer/id #uuid "214151cc-952c-569b-98a8-4a08d79a4188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368991} {:answer/id #uuid "c53bc063-57b1-57ac-a505-ffa15102e179" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0bd0fc6-bb96-5a85-9066-598aa3452b77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368988} :answer-field/id #uuid "03e2c16d-6fb0-5b77-a53e-24acc37a3251" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368987}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "101d2691-d73f-5028-af43-74b860b5e6e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-39239" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We have a decoupled system. Therefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =-1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce35e5a9-2444-5e5f-9463-5a4d54496d9d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a Decoupled Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "885be0a2-3978-5a25-9895-cc1204770ea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3\\pi t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\pi t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368995} {:answer/id #uuid "2f224680-ef8d-5b70-935b-88353ea92b94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\pi t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368996} {:answer/id #uuid "2c3cdb8e-fd03-57e6-87c7-7b576f58f5da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3\\pi t},\\,{c}_{1}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368997} {:answer/id #uuid "09c13599-1cd2-5401-95a0-2254141a6810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3\\pi t},\\,{c}_{1}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368998} {:answer/id #uuid "323741c4-b32f-599e-adf2-02c25e38c5c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\pi t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "323741c4-b32f-599e-adf2-02c25e38c5c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\pi t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368999} :answer-field/id #uuid "75aecd08-3203-57dd-962d-39e719c426fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bcd1cc12-d6f9-5379-af7f-a875b90aaa40" :question/math-academy-id "q-39703" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations\n${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=\\pi {x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}$" :question/worked-solution "Given a decoupled system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {\\lambda }_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write our differential equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\pi \\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSince the matrix of the differential system is diagonal, the system is decoupled. \n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\pi t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce35e5a9-2444-5e5f-9463-5a4d54496d9d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a Decoupled Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fcab45ec-6fc0-515e-b077-0059094c10e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-et},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369002} {:answer/id #uuid "891b28cb-d4f5-596d-b1e2-38fb8645eafa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{et}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369003} {:answer/id #uuid "db34ab3e-a262-5b78-903c-758fcd6072bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369004} {:answer/id #uuid "e278da2f-c598-5824-9df6-71b8f5e48586" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{et}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369005} {:answer/id #uuid "0228f297-9639-5895-be34-da7d75d89a4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answ